      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "232fc51c-a784-5a0a-ab11-96190800b2c3",
        ":question/problem": "If $tan\u2061x=\\frac{1}{3},$ for some value of $x,$ find the value of $12tan\u2061(x+5\\pi )-6.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=tan\u2061x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ntan\u2061x=tan\u2061(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan\u2061x=tan\u2061(x+5\\cdot \\pi )=tan\u2061(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $tan\u2061x=\\frac{1}{3},$ we get that $tan\u2061(x+5\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n12tan\u2061(x+5\\pi )-6=12(\\frac{1}{3})-6=4-6=-2.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
